The '''1994 New Hampshire gubernatorial election''' took place on November 8, 1994. [[Incumbent]] [[Governor of New Hampshire|Governor]] [[Steve Merrill]] won re-election to a second term in a [[Landslide victory|landslide]] amidst the concurrent [[Republican Revolution]]. 

Despite his high popularity as governor, Merrill chose not to seek a third term in [[1996 New Hampshire gubernatorial election|1996]], citing wanting to spend more time with his wife and kids.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Times |first=The New York |date=1996-04-04 |title=POLITICS: TIME OUT;New Hampshire Governor Backs Away From Politics |url=https://www.nytimes.com/1996/04/04/us/politics-time-out-new-hampshire-governor-backs-away-from-politics.html |access-date=2026-04-11 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Following this election, Democrats would control the governorship for 18 of the next 20 years.

